\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  \cf0 Almighty God who gave us all things
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 you gave to us this whole wide world
\par for us to use as our earthly home;
\par  You care for us as our father
\par and you abundantly bless us
\par O' who on earth is just like you.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  All, who today come to your table
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj How can someone ever count them
\par But whatever He gives them to eat
\par shall be sufficient for them all
\par the food that your children consume
\par comes from the hands of Lord our God.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  Your children plant in a happy mood
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj and it bear fruits in its own time.
\par The sun shines over the rains come  down
\par in every corner of the world
\par It is by thy great power and might
\par and you remember all thy works
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.    What  then, O God, can we think about
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0  of all the wondrous things you do?
\par   No human can ever be like you
\par   Your talent are in no measure
\par  we do not befit none of them
\par  all these good things you give to us.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.    So we shall never be forgetful
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj  that you gave us all your blessings
\par  whatever food that we have to eat
\par  shows that great love you have for us
\par  Our hearts and all that of our mouth
\par  shall give you thanks, Almighty God
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

